card "Shibboleth"
  side: runner
  type: program
  subtypes: Icebreaker, Decoder
  cost: 1
  strength: 3
  memory: 1
  faction: Criminal
  set: The Automata Initiative
  text:
    Threat 4 → This program gets −2 strength. (This ability is active if any player has 4 or more agenda points.)
    Interface → 1[credit]: Break 1 code gate subroutine.
    2[credit]: +2 strength.
  # The `static threat 4:` block this sentence wants is written and denotes
  # correctly, but `Vm::char_effects` does not consult 9.3.6f, so the −2 would
  # apply at every threat level — a wrong card, not a partial one. See the gap
  # list in docs/vm/WAVES.md.
  unimplemented: "Threat 4 → This program gets −2 strength."
  paid interface 1 credit:
    break 1 code gate subroutine
  paid 2 credits:
    +2 strength

card "Cupellation"
  side: runner
  type: program
  cost: 1
  strength: 0
  memory: 1
  faction: Criminal
  set: Rebellion Without Rehearsal
  text:
    Limit 1 hosted card.
    Access → 1[credit]: Host the non-agenda card you are accessing faceup on this program. (If it was installed, it becomes uninstalled.)
    Whenever you breach HQ, if this program has a hosted Corp card, you may pay 1[credit] and trash this program to access 2 additional cards.
  # `limit 1 hosted card` is written and denotes into StaticDecl::CanHost, but
  # 1.13.6b's exclusion is derived by scanning for a self-hosting instruction —
  # and this card's own hosting ability is not sayable yet, so the capacity
  # declaration would become an install permission. See docs/vm/WAVES.md.
  unimplemented: "Limit 1 hosted card."
  unimplemented: "Access → 1[credit]: Host the non-agenda card you are accessing faceup on this program."
  unimplemented: "Whenever you breach HQ, if this program has a hosted Corp card, you may pay 1[credit] and trash this program to access 2 additional cards."

